      },
      "worked": "Split the hexagon into six equilateral triangles of side length 2. Bisect one triangle; its half-base is 1. Let its height be $h$.\n$$\\begin{align*}h^2+1^2&=2^2\\\\h^2+1&=4\\\\h^2&=3\\\\h&=\\sqrt{3}\\\\A_{\\text{triangle}}&=\\frac{1}{2}\\times2\\times\\sqrt{3}\\\\A_{\\text{triangle}}&=\\sqrt{3}\\\\A_{\\text{hexagon}}&=6\\times\\sqrt{3}\\\\A_{\\text{hexagon}}&=6\\sqrt{3}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
